From 8ac0861788d5247d63f6d6be090170d6e9492e21 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 01:47:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Blu-ray] Simulate a 3D display, for 3D discs that need one,
 off by default

Some Blu-ray 3D discs do not start, or stay on a black screen, on a player
that says that its display has no 3D (SamuriHL measured Frozen 3D stopping
on a playlist of one still picture with PSR24 set and PSR21/PSR23 saying 2D,
which is what Kodi tells a 3D disc on a display without 3D).
A setting in the Blu-ray group of Player > Discs: bluray.hadessimulate3d,
"Simulate a 3D display", off by default (level 2).

On, a disc that declares 3D content is left to find the player and the
display of 3D where the second view is not wanted: the profile is held back
as it is where the second view is wanted (KODI::MULTIVIEW::Persona3D()), and
libbluray gives the disc its own registers of 3D when it reads the index
(psr_init_3D(): profile 5 v2.4, PSR21 3D preferred, PSR23 the four 3D
capabilities of the display, PSR22 the disc's initial mode). Its second view
is still not read (DiscSecondView() is unchanged), so the disc takes its way
for 3D and plays its base view in 2D. A disc without 3D content gets the
profile once it is open, as before; with the setting off, or where the
second view is wanted, nothing changes.

kodi.log says, for a 3D disc with the setting on, that it was told of a
player and a display of 3D and plays in 2D. Spanish through Estuary
(#32340, #32341; es_es, es_ar, es_mx) and CGUIUtils::GetHadesString().
Idea: SamuriHL's bluray.simulate3ddisplay.
